# Ni no Kuni DS - operator session (Phase-5Z), frame-timed input script
# replay: NNK_INPUT_FILE=this NNK_GX=headless NNK_STEP_LIMIT=<n> ./nnk_runner
# frame = DISPLAY frame (gxd_frames); mask = active-low KEYINPUT
#   idle 0x3FF | A=0x3FE B=0x3FD Select=0x3FB Start=0x3F7
#   D-pad Right=0x3EF Left=0x3DF Up=0x3BF Down=0x37F | R=0x2FF L=0x1FF
# Start every 36 frames (advance one prompt) from frame 13,
# then DS A at frame 917 = the operator's movie skip (~510M steps).
#
# WARNING (Phase-5AD, measured): this script SKIPS THE INTRO MOVIE.
#   The movie player leaves its frame loop on an A|Start edge (0x0207D230 -
#   0x0207D248, overlay 13).  With this script the game enters the movie player
#   at display frame 578, presents 7 frames, and the press at frame 589 ends the
#   session at master step 327,550,216: the Mobiclip splash and the intro movie
#   are never shown, and the band f3700..f4300 stays flat black (both screens).
#   For a band/acceptance measurement run WITHOUT this file (or with a schedule
#   that has no presses after the movie window): see PHASE5AD.md.
